{"entryId":"1675","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1675:1","sourceSha256":"5d0ec89915271917ef25602b3525cca3d0fad94482febc59597cdd0933a66a07","englishSha256":"cb8c0169c985fc40547db27e557bd71bc7c08c78eb3d872b87945efbe2fd1151","citations":[{"id":"1675:1:citation-01","he":[14,32],"en":[22,43],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_72b.1"},"reference":"Eruvin 72b:1","assessment":"The Bavli gives Rabbi Yehudah HaSabbar’s statement about partitions and a common eruv.","evidence":[{"reference":"Eruvin 72b:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_72b.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1675:1:citation-02","he":[33,62],"en":[45,59],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Eruvin_72b.1.1"},"reference":"Rashi on Eruvin 72b:1:1","assessment":"Rashi explicitly attributes the epithet to his sharpness.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Eruvin 72b:1:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Eruvin_72b.1.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1675:1:citation-03","he":[65,70],"en":[103,108],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sefer_HeArukh%2C_Letter_Samekh_26"},"reference":"Sefer HeArukh, Letter Samekh 26","assessment":"Arukh and Rif explicitly give HaSabbakh. Arukh’s lemma is sabkha and the surrounding definitions concern a head covering. Arukh’s printed folio number differs from the checked Bavli.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sefer HeArukh, Letter Samekh 26","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sefer_HeArukh%2C_Letter_Samekh_26"},"witness":"Sefer HeArukh, Lublin 1883"},{"reference":"Rif Eruvin 22a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rif_Eruvin_22a.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"1675:1:citation-04","he":[71,76],"en":[113,121],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rif_Eruvin_22a.2"},"reference":"Rif Eruvin 22a:2","assessment":"Arukh and Rif explicitly give HaSabbakh. Arukh’s lemma is sabkha and the surrounding definitions concern a head covering. Arukh’s printed